      "message": "fix(multiaxis): new angles on a legacy tilt take the current frame basis\n\nA tilt loaded from a file without basis_version keeps the pre-#2133\nframe basis 0. The operation page and MCP edit_operation kept that\nbasis when the user set new angles. At A0/B180 the basis-0 frame turns\nplane X to world Y, so a slot from (10,0) to (30,0) posted\nG1 X0 Y-10 -> X0 Y-30 where a new operation posts X10 Y0 -> X30 Y0.\n\nEditOperationParams now steps the basis to 1 when the edit changes the\nA or B angle. An edit that keeps the angles keeps basis 0, and an\nunedited old file posts what it posted before (tilt_basis_compat).\n\nFixes #2599\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
